  "provider_query": "Find the public X status from OpenAI that announces GPT-4",
  "answer": "The official OpenAI post announcing GPT-4 is from **14 March 2023**.\n\n1. **@OpenAI** — “Announcing GPT-4, a large multimodal model, with our best-ever results on capabilities and alignment.”  \n   https://x.com/OpenAI/status/1635687373060317185  \n   Posted 2023-03-14 ~17:00 UTC. [web:0] [web:10]\n\nRelated posts from OpenAI leadership the same day:\n\n2. **@gdb** (Greg Brockman) — “We’re releasing GPT-4 — a large multimodal model…”  \n   https://x.com/gdb/status/1635687252616679426  \n   2023-03-14 ~17:00 UTC. [web:4] [web:11]\n\n3. **@sama** (Sam Altman) — “here is GPT-4, our most capable and aligned model yet… available today in our API (with a waitlist) and in ChatGPT+.”  \n   https://x.com/sama/status/1635687859494715393 (thread starts around this time)  \n   2023-03-14 ~17:02 UTC. [web:7] [web:15]\n\n4. **@miramurati** (Mira Murati) — “Unveiling GPT-4 — our large multimodal model…”  \n   https://x.com/miramurati/status/1635688069692293121  \n   2023-03-14 ~17:03 UTC. [web:3] [web:12]\n\n5. **@npew** (Peter Welinder, OpenAI) — “GPT-4 is here: our smartest and most reliable model yet!”  \n   https://x.com/npew/status/1635687624047489024  \n   2023-03-14 ~17:01 UTC. [web:13]\n\nCoverage and reactions (not the OpenAI account):\n\n6. **@verge** — “OpenAI announces GPT-4 — the next generation of its AI language model.”  \n   https://x.com/verge/status/1635688829792268307  \n   2023-03-14 ~17:06 UTC. [web:2] [web:17]\n\n7. **@rowancheung** — “It’s here. OpenAI just launched GPT-4.” (thread linking the research post and API waitlist)  \n   https://x.com/rowancheung/status/1635691542739574784  \n   2023-03-14 ~17:14–17:17 UTC. [web:6]\n\n8. **@tomwarren** — notes that OpenAI had just announced GPT-4 (image or text input).  \n   https://x.com/tomwarren/status/1635690339926257677  \n   2023-03-14 ~17:12 UTC. [web:16]\n\nThe canonical public announcement from the OpenAI account is status **1635687373060317185**.",
